## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a governed lakehouse with explicit contracts, provenance, and cross-tenant isolation under schema drift pressure.

## Key Concepts
- Data contracts and evolving schemas
- Per-file provenance auditing
- CDC-like upserts in Delta Lake
- Unity Catalog RBAC with masking
- Drift detection and drift-violation views
- Late-data handling and cross-region DR
- Synthetic data/testing strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo contract check
function validateContract(schema, record) {
  // ensure required fields exist and types match
  for (const [field, type] of Object.entries(schema.fields)) {
    if (!(field in record)) return false;
    if (typeof record[field] !== type) return false;
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema evolution across multiple tenants without breaking dashboards?
- What failure scenarios could break the Data Contract Registry and how would you mitigate?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes cross-region DR, evolving schemas, and strict data contracts in real-time Databricks workloads, plus governance via Unity Catalog.

## Key Concepts

- Auto Loader for scalable ingestion with schema evolution
- Delta Live Tables for pipeline quality, CDC, and contracts
- Cross-region replication and Delta time travel
- Unity Catalog RBAC and row-level security
- Schema drift handling with zero-downtime strategies
- Lightweight test harness with synthetic data

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo contract check in a Delta Live Tables-like stage
function checkContract(row) {
  if (!row.event_id || !row.schema_version) {
    throw new Error("Contract violation");
  }
  return row;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect drift and auto-heal without downtime?
- How would you rollback a run while preserving lineage and metadata?
